  "proof_observations": {
    "gate_only_fractional_tuple": "Two isolated weak gates vanish at selectors(1/2,1/2), zero copies; two guard-free homogeneous branches would violate disjointness, so this is not a counterexample to the complete theorem.",
    "natural_nonzero_input": "Nonnegative summands vanish; two positive selectors force every local input copy zero, contradicting X!=0. Unique selected copy equals integer X, so guard slacks and output are integers.",
    "no_universal_scalar_improvement": "Nothing in these notes gives an ordinary unbounded fixed-arity compiler or a new paid operation count.",
    "partial_map_scope": "Undefined collisions/no next event produce no branch. PQC unconditioned clipped trace is total and has one zero; signal endpoint fibre may be empty. Both horizons are external.",
    "zero_input": "Input-copy equations and nonnegativity force all copies zero. Each strict-guard branch has selector zero. All equality/weak-only homogeneous branches contain zero; disjointness on N^d permits at most one. Selector sum then forces one, or no solution. Thus complete real fibres over natural X are integral also at X=0."
  },
  "scope": "new semantic text only, base..head; unchanged source theorem context and prior reviews consulted; no code suites, TeX builds, PDF QA, external-literature re-review, or later commit audit",
